# Table of pmi for DEGAS-2

$Id$

# Interaction between particles (species) and materials to produce 
# other particles.
# Each interaction is represented by four logical lines:
# (1) the full name of the reaction.  
# (2) the second is a blank-delimited sequence of entries of the form
# name particle + material + ... => particle + particle + ...
#     Note that:
#          - particles are neutral; each pmi will be assumed to treat ions
#          - the material is listed second
#          - the material is not repeated on the right side
#          - if the particle symbols are intended to represent their isotopic
#            equivalents as well, use "->" instead of "=>"
# (3) the file name with probabilities and product distributions
# (4) the type of interaction

hydrogen reflection (ruzic) on carbon
hreflc H + C => H
../data/hreflc.nc 
reflection

deuterium reflection (ruzic) on carbon
dreflc D + C => D
../data/dreflc.nc 
reflection

tritium reflection (ruzic) on carbon
treflc T + C => T
../data/treflc.nc
reflection

hydrogen reflection (marlowe) on iron
hreflfe H + Fe => H
../data/hreflfe.nc
reflection

helium reflection (marlowe) on iron
hereflfe He + Fe => He
../data/hereflfe.nc
reflection

hydrogen reflection (ruzic) on molybdenum
hreflmo H + mo => H
../data/hreflmo.nc 
reflection

deuterium reflection (ruzic) on molybdenum
dreflmo D + mo => D
../data/dreflmo.nc 
reflection

deuterium reflection (trim) on molybdenum
D_refl_strim_Mo D + mo => D
../data/D_refl_strim_Mo.nc 
reflection

hydrogen reflection on mirror
hmirror H + mirror -> H
../data/hmirror.nc
reflection

hydrogen molecule reflection on mirror
h2mirror H2 + mirror -> H2
../data/h2mirror.nc
reflection

hydrogen adsorption on carbon
hadsorbc H + C ->
../data/hadsorbc.nc
adsorption

hydrogen molecule adsorption on carbon
h2adsorbc H2 + C -> 
../data/h2adsorbc.nc
adsorption

hydrogen desorption from carbon
hdesorbc H + C -> H + H2
../data/hdesorbc.nc
desorption

hydrogen molecule desorption from carbon
h2desorbc H2 + C -> H2
../data/h2desorbc.nc
desorption

